13382.sol:
If resultant of two unit vectors is unit vector, then angle between them is $\frac{2 \pi}{3}$, so $\begin{aligned}
|\mathbf{a}-\mathbf{b}|^2 & =|a|^2+|b|^2-2|\mathbf{a}||\mathbf{b}| \cos \frac{2 \pi}{3}$\\
& =1+1-2(1)(1)(-1 / 2)=2+1=3 .
\end{aligned}

